 # bench-sleep-tool (benchmark fixture)
 
-A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool, written in the 0.1.1-era style
-(bare `cordis` cohort). The host is moving to dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
+A tiny tool plugin exposing one `sleep` tool, written for the dsh
+0.1.2-alpha.2 cohort: `@deepseek-ai/cordis` runtime types,
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-tools` registration and `ToolRunContext`, and the
+`@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm` `ContentBlock`. The 0.1.1-era sources were migrated to
+this cohort (bare `cordis` and the `dsh-tools` `ContentBlock` re-export no
+longer exist on the host).
+
+Capabilities (as shipped):
+
+- the model-facing `sleep` tool, cancellable through the tool call's
+  `exec.signal`;
+- a per-call duration budget from plugin config: `maxDurationMs` (default
+  60000, caps one sleep) and `defaultDurationMs` (default 0, used when the
+  model omits `duration_ms`);
+- the bundle layer: `cordis.patch.yml` (declared as `dsh.bundle.patch` in
+  package.json) inserts the plugin row with those defaults.
 
 Release procedure (internal):
 
